ria-controls=\"VPNavScreen\" data-v-c248beec=\"\" data-v-0bb9094f=\"\"><span class=\"container\" data-v-0bb9094f=\"\"><span class=\"top\" data-v-0bb9094f=\"\"></span><span class=\"middle\" data-v-0bb9094f=\"\"></span><span class=\"bottom\" data-v-0bb9094f=\"\"></span></span></button></div></div></div></div><div class=\"divider\" data-v-c248beec=\"\"><div class=\"divider-line\" data-v-c248beec=\"\"></div></div></div><!----></header><div class=\"VPLocalNav has-sidebar empty\" data-v-51608ad5=\"\" data-v-b185fc59=\"\"><div class=\"container\" data-v-b185fc59=\"\"><button class=\"menu\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"VPSidebarNav\" data-v-b185fc59=\"\"><span class=\"vpi-align-left menu-icon\" data-v-b185fc59=\"\"></span><span class=\"menu-text\" data-v-b185fc59=\"\">Menu</span></button><div class=\"VPLocalNavOutlineDropdown\" style=\"--vp-vh:0px;\" data-v-b185fc59=\"\" data-v-9bbff571=\"\"><button data-v-9bbff571=\"\">Return to top</button><!----></div></div></div><aside class=\"VPSidebar\" data-v-51608ad5=\"\" data-v-f14c4045=\"\"><div class=\"curtain\" data-v-f14c4045=\"\"></div><nav class=\"nav\" id=\"VPSidebarNav\" aria-labelledby=\"sidebar-aria-label\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-v-f14c4045=\"\"><span class=\"visually-hidden\" id=\"sidebar-aria-label\" data-v-f14c4045=\"\"> Sidebar Navigation </span><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><div class=\"no-transition group\" data-v-fd2cbcf3=\"\"><section class=\"VPSidebarItem level-0 has-active\" data-v-fd2cbcf3=\"\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"item\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"indicator\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"></div><h2 class=\"text\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\">Guide</h2><!----></div><div class=\"items\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><!--[--><div class=\"VPSidebarItem level-1 is-link\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"item\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"indicator\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"></div><a class=\"VPLink link link\" href=\"/smartclass-dispatchub/guide/getting-started\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><!--[--><p class=\"text\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\">Getting Started</p><!--]--></a><!----></div><!----></div><div class=\"VPSidebarItem level-1 is-link\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"item\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"indicator\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"></div><a class=\"VPLink link link\" href=\"/smartclass-dispatchub/guide/deploy\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><!--[--><p class=\"text\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\">Deployment</p><!--]--></a><!----></div><!----></div><div class=\"VPSidebarItem level-1 is-link\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"item\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"indicator\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"></div><a class=\"VPLink link link\" href=\"/smartclass-dispatchub/guide/permissions\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><!--[--><p class=\"text\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\">Permissions</p><!--]--></a><!----></div><!----></div><div class=\"VPSidebarItem level-1 is-link\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"item\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"indicator\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"></div><a class=\"VPLink link link\" href=\"/smartclass-dispatchub/guide/api-usage\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><!--[--><p class=\"text\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\">API Usage</p><!--]--></a><!----></div><!----></div><div class=\"VPSidebarItem level-1 is-link\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"item\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"indicator\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"></div><a class=\"VPLink link link\" href=\"/smartclass-dispatchub/guide/operations\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><!--[--><p class=\"text\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\">Operations</p><!--]--></a><!----></div><!----></div><!--]--></div></section></div><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--></nav></aside><div class=\"VPContent has-sidebar\" id=\"VPContent\" data-v-51608ad5=\"\" data-v-22444a1e=\"\"><div class=\"VPDoc has-sidebar has-aside\" data-v-22444a1e=\"\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><!--[--><!--]--><div class=\"container\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><div class=\"aside\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><div class=\"aside-curtain\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"></div><div class=\"aside-container\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><div class=\"aside-content\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><div class=\"VPDocAside\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\" data-v-871b5275=\"\"><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--><nav aria-labelledby=\"doc-outline-aria-label\" class=\"VPDocAsideOutline\" data-v-871b5275=\"\" data-v-d607fa03=\"\"><div class=\"content\" data-v-d607fa03=\"\"><div class=\"outline-marker\" data-v-d607fa03=\"\"></div><div aria-level=\"2\" class=\"outline-title\" id=\"doc-outline-aria-label\" role=\"heading\" data-v-d607fa03=\"\">On this page</div><ul class=\"VPDocOutlineItem root\" data-v-d607fa03=\"\" data-v-41a17517=\"\"><!--[--><!--]--></ul></div></nav><!--[--><!--]--><div class=\"spacer\" data-v-871b5275=\"\"></div><!--[--><!--]--><!----><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--></div></div></div></div><div class=\"content\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><div class=\"content-container\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><!--[--><!--]--><main class=\"main\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><div style=\"position:relative;\" class=\"vp-doc _smartclass-dispatchub_guide_permissions\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><div><h1 id=\"permissions\" tabindex=\"-1\">Permissions <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#permissions\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Permissions&quot;\">​</a></h1><p>Every <code>/api/v1</code> call is authenticated and authorized through <a href=\"https://github.com/crazy4chicken/nsc-teamusers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">teamusers</a>. dispatchub keeps no local accounts: it verifies the bearer token locally against the issuer's JWKS and then resolves the caller's permissions <strong>remotely on every request</strong> - permissions are never carried inside the token.</p><h2 id=\"the-teamusers-model\" tabindex=\"-1\">The teamusers model <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#the-teamusers-model\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;The teamusers model&quot;\">​</a></h2><ul><li>teamusers is an Ed25519 (EdDSA) JWT issuer. Its JWKS lives at <code>{base}/.well-known/jwks.json</code>; access tokens are short-lived (TTL 600 s by default).</li><li>Sign-in is <code>POST /auth/login {username,password}</code> and returns an access token and a refresh token. Services instead use <code>POST /auth/client-credentials {client_id,client_secret}</code>.</li><li>A principal is a user <code>{id, username, display_name, ...}</code> plus an optional team. There is <strong>no teacher/class/campus model</strong> in teamusers: courses, rooms and teachers are dispatchub's own data.</li><li>A permission is a three-segment key, matched literally segment by segment. The only wildcard is <code>*</code>, which matches exactly one segment.</li></ul><h2 id=\"the-nine-keys\" tabindex=\"-1\">The nine keys <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#the-nine-keys\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;The nine keys&quot;\">​</a></h2><p>dispatchub's catalog consists of three independent permissions, each with three scopes. None implies another:</p><table tabindex=\"0\"><thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Grants</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>dispatch:read:&lt;scope&gt;</code></td><td>Read terms, rooms, import history, sessions, artifacts and live room status.</td></tr><tr><td><code>dispatch:manage:&lt;scope&gt;</code></td><td>Create/update terms and 节次 tables; bind and unbind rooms; import timetables.</td></tr><tr><td><code>dispatch:control:&lt;scope&gt;</code></td><td>Start and stop recordings, switch cameras, take snapshots.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>In full:</p><div class=\"language-text vp-adaptive-theme\"><button title=\"Copy Code\" class=\"copy\"></button><span class=\"lang\">text</span><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>dispatch:read:any     dispatch:read:team     dispatch:read:own</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>dispatch:manage:any   dispatch:manage:team   dispatch:manage:own     # terms, rooms, imports</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>dispatch:control:any  dispatch:control:team  dispatch:control:own    # recording, camera switch, photo</span></span></code></pre></div><p>A teacher who records their own lessons needs <code>dispatch:read</code> <strong>and</strong> <code>dispatch:control</code> at <code>own</code> or <code>team</code> scope; an operator console needs <code>dispatch:read:any</code> plus <code>dispatch:control:any</code>; the administrator who maintains rooms and imports needs <code>dispatch:manage</code> as well.</p><h2 id=\"the-scope-ladder\" tabindex=\"-1\">The scope ladder <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#the-scope-ladder\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;The scope ladder&quot;\">​</a></h2><p>For every request dispatchub loads the target room (or the session's room) and builds the candidate key list broadest-first:</p><div class=\"language-text vp-adaptive-theme\"><button title=\"Copy Code\" class=\"copy\"></button><span class=\"lang\">text</span><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>keys = [\"dispatch:&lt;action&gt;:any\"]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>if room.team_id  != \"\" and room.team_id  == claims.team:    keys += [\"dispatch:&lt;action&gt;:team\"]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>if room.owner_id != \"\" and room.owner_id == claims.subject: keys += [\"dispatch:&lt;action&gt;:own\"]</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The first candidate the caller is allowed to use wins. None is implied by another:</p><ul><li><code>any</code> needs no relationship to the room.</li><li><code>team</code> is only considered when the room's <code>team_id</code> equals the caller's <code>team</code>.</li><li><code>own</code> is only considered when the room's <code>owner_id</code> equals the caller's <code>sub</code>.</li></ul><p><code>team_id</code> and <code>owner_id</code> are <strong>snapshotted onto the room row when the binding is created</strong> (<code>PUT /api/v1/rooms/{room_code}</code> reads them from the webcam-server device). That is why the binding is the source of truth for scope resolution: if the device's ownership changes upstream, re-bind the room to refresh the snapshot.</p><p>Collection and creation routes (<code>GET /api/v1/rooms</code>, <code>GET /api/v1/sessions</code>, <code>GET/POST /api/v1/terms</code> and the import routes) have no single room to compare against, so no <code>team</code>/<code>own</code> candidate is ever built for them: they require the <code>any</code>-scoped key (<code>dispatch:read:any</code> or <code>dispatch:manage:any</code>).</p><p>One route is a hybrid: <code>PUT /api/v1/rooms/{room_code}</code> treats a missing room as a create, so a <strong>new</strong> binding has no ownership snapshot and only <code>dispatch:manage:any</code> can grant it. Re-binding an <strong>existing</strong> room keeps its snapshot and accepts <code>dispatch:manage:team</code> / <code>dispatch:manage:own</code> through the same ladder.</p><h2 id=\"endpoint-matrix\" tabindex=\"-1\">Endpoint matrix <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#endpoint-matrix\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Endpoint matrix&quot;\">​</a></h2><p><code>&lt;scope&gt;</code> resolves through the ladder above.</p><table tabindex=\"0\"><thead><tr><th>Route</th><th>Permission</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>GET /api/v1/terms</code>, <code>POST /api/v1/terms</code></td><td><code>dispatch:read:&lt;scope&gt;</code> / <code>dispatch:manage:&lt;scope&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /api/v1/terms/{term_code}/periods</code>, <code>PUT .../periods</code></td><td><code>dispatch:read:&lt;scope&gt;</code> / <code>dispatch:manage:&lt;scope&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /api/v1/rooms</code></td><td><code>dispatch:read:&lt;scope&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>PUT /api/v1/rooms/{room_code}</code>, <code>DELETE /api/v1/rooms/{room_code}</code></td><td><code>dispatch:manage:&lt;scope&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /api/v1/timetable/imports</code></td><td><code>dispatch:manage:&lt;scope&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /api/v1/timetable/imports</code>, <code>GET /api/v1/timetable/imports/{id}</code></td><td><code>dispatch:read:&lt;scope&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /api/v1/sessions</code>, <code>GET /api/v1/sessions/{id}</code>, <code>GET /api/v1/sessions/{id}/artifacts</code></td><td><code>dispatch:read:&lt;scope&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /api/v1/sessions/{id}/recording/start</code>, <code>POST /api/v1/sessions/{id}/recording/stop</code></td><td><code>dispatch:control:&lt;scope&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /api/v1/rooms/{room_code}/recording/start</code>, <code>POST /api/v1/rooms/{room_code}/recording/stop</code></td><td><code>dispatch:control:&lt;scope&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /api/v1/rooms/{room_code}/camera/switch</code></td><td><code>dispatch:control:&lt;scope&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /api/v1/rooms/{room_code}/photo</code></td><td><code>dispatch:control:&lt;scope&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /api/v1/rooms/{room_code}/live</code></td><td><code>dispatch:read:&lt;scope&gt;</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p><code>GET /healthz</code> and <code>GET /readyz</code> are public.</p><p>The generated <a href=\"/smartclass-dispatchub/api/overview\">API reference</a> repeats the permission for each operation through its <code>x-teamusers-permission</code> extension, which lists the <code>any</code> and <code>team</code> keys an endpoint accepts; because that extension has only those two slots, the <code>own</code> scope is documented on this page only.</p><h2 id=\"failure-shapes\" tabindex=\"-1\">Failure shapes <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#failure-shapes\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Failure shapes&quot;\">​</a></h2><table tabindex=\"0\"><thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>Response</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Missing, malformed or unverifiable token</td><td><code>401</code> with the teamusers decision body <code>{\"allow\": false, \"reason\": \"...\"}</code> and <code>WWW-Authenticate: Bearer realm=\"teamusers\"</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>Verified caller, no candidate key allowed</td><td><code>403</code> RFC 9457 problem detail with <code>detail: \"permission denied\"</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>teamusers unreachable or erroring</td><td><code>503</code> problem detail - dispatchub <strong>fails closed</strong>, never allows.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id=\"catalog-registration\" tabindex=\"-1\">Catalog registration <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#catalog-registration\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Catalog registration&quot;\">​</a></h2><p>A permission key must exist in teamusers' catalog before a role can carry it. Register all nine once per deployment - either with the service subcommand:</p><div class=\"language-sh vp-adaptive-theme\"><button title=\"Copy Code\" class=\"copy\"></button><span class=\"lang\">sh</span><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;\">dispatchub</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\"> register-permissions</span></span></code></pre></div><p>which upserts each key with <code>POST /permissions/ {key, description, registered_by}</code>, or by hand:</p><div class=\"language-sh vp-adaptive-theme\"><button title=\"Copy Code\" class=\"copy\"></button><span class=\"lang\">sh</span><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">TEAMUSERS_URL</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">http://127.0.0.1:8082</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">TEAMUSERS_ADMIN_TOKEN</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">'&lt;teamusers admin token&gt;'</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;\">for</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\"> key </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;\">in</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">  dispatch:read:any</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\"> dispatch:read:team</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\"> dispatch:read:own</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">  dispatch:manage:any</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\"> dispatch:manage:team</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\"> dispatch:manage:own</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">  dispatch:control:any</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\"> dispatch:control:team</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\"> dispatch:control:own</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;\">do</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;\">  curl</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\"> -sS</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\"> -X</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\"> POST</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\"> \"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">$TEAMUSERS_URL</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">/permissions/\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">    -H</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\"> \"Authorization: Bearer </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">$TEAMUSERS_ADMIN_TOKEN</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">    -H</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\"> 'Content-Type: application/json'</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">    --data</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\"> \"{</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">\\\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">key</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">\\\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">\\\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">$key</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">\\\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">,</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">\\\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">description</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">\\\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">\\\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">SmartClass dispatch hub</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">\\\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">,</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">\\\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">registered_by</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">\\\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">\\\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">smartclass-dispatchub</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">\\\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">}\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;\">done</span></span></code></pre></div><p>As a shorthand, one wildcard key per action (<code>dispatch:read:*</code>, <code>dispatch:manage:*</code>, <code>dispatch:control:*</code>) can be registered instead and bound wherever all three scoped keys would have been.</p><h2 id=\"service-credential\" tabindex=\"-1\">Service credential <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#service-credential\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Service credential&quot;\">​</a></h2><p>dispatchub is itself a teamusers client. Its credential - <code>DISPATCH_TEAMUSERS_CLIENT_ID</code> / <code>DISPATCH_TEAMUSERS_CLIENT_SECRET</code> - authenticates the remote permission lookups behind every inbound request, and the same credential is exchanged for the outbound tokens used to call smartclass-webcam-server. The access token is cached and refreshed before it expires; a <code>401</code> from webcam-server triggers exactly one forced refresh and retry.</p><p>For dispatchub to command webcam-server, the credential's principal must be bound to a role that carries every <code>cam:*</code> key dispatchub uses. The union of the scope ladders it walks means the practical requirement is:</p><ul><li><code>cam:read:any</code> (device, stream, photo and segment reads)</li><li><code>cam:control:any</code> (recording start/stop, camera switch, snapshot)</li></ul><p>Without them webcam-server answers <code>403</code> and the affected sessions fail with <code>upstream_unavailable</code>/<code>permission denied</code> details.</p><h2 id=\"teacher-identity\" tabindex=\"-1\">Teacher identity <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#teacher-identity\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Teacher identity&quot;\">​</a></h2><p><code>teacher_username</code> is stored verbatim from the CSV. Where a token <code>sub</code> is needed - <code>own</code> scope, audit fields - dispatchub resolves it through a <code>teamusers_identities(username, subject_id, synced_at)</code> cache, filled on first successful lookup. If teamusers has no username-to-subject lookup endpoint available, <code>teacher_user_id</code> stays <code>NULL</code> and <code>own</code>-scoped access for that teacher degrades to <code>team</code>/<code>any</code>. This is a known open item; verify the lookup endpoint in your phase 0 before promising per-teacher self-service.</p></div></div></main><footer class=\"VPDocFooter\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\"><!--[--><!--]--><div class=\"edit-info\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\"><!----><div class=\"last-updated\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\"><p class=\"VPLastUpdated\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\" data-v-3104ff47=\"\">Last updated: <time datetime=\"2026-10-05T12:46:33.000Z\" data-v-3104ff47=\"\"></time></p></div></div><nav class=\"prev-next\" aria-labelledby=\"doc-footer-aria-label\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\"><span class=\"visually-hidden\" id=\"doc-footer-aria-label\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\">Pager</span><div class=\"pager\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\"><a class=\"VPLink link pager-link prev\" href=\"/smartclass-dispatchub/guide/deploy\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\"><!--[--><span class=\"desc\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\">Previous page</span><span class=\"title\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\">Deployment</span><!--]--></a></div><div class=\"pager\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\"><a class=\"VPLink link pager-link next\" href=\"/smartclass-dispatchub/guid